host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The address-space debt splits, and the arithmetic half is paid whole
prompt Kyri first, then REMEMBER and the itineraries, Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; each lap deep-reads one council-rota row.
think Standfast first. Every living REDS row reads CLOSED -- %122 (the shared exclusion list, the council rota rotted in a name's blind spot) and %123 (the nib guard reading positionally) both carry closure notes with witnesses on metal. One item stands surfaced rather than open: four cairn nibs live on no remote, which is Keaton's word by construction since pushing them would republish tissue a debride removed. The line was clear for new work.
think Rota row 4 this lap -- Earth and Mercury, the concrete: the one-clock naming law, Two Rooms, the marked value. Two Rooms is the one that earned its place today: a claim enters the checkable room only when a witness binds it, and everything below was written so the witness could bind it before the prose claimed it.
think The running thread pointed clearly. The newest log's recommend line named the address-space debt as the next constructive door and called it a design round, since a page table is a machine fact and a hosted supervisor has no address space to build.
think Reading that sentence a second time is what this round is. It is true and it is half true. An address space is a DECISION -- which pages cover a span, at which sizes, over how many levels of tree -- and an ACT -- writing entries into real memory, assigning an identifier, invoking a retype. The act wants a kernel. The decision wants nothing but arithmetic over five numbers seL4 publishes in a header we may read.
think So the debt splits, and the pure half is the larger one. Read the five numbers off vendor/sel4's riscv64 constants.h rather than from memory: page 12 bits, large 21, huge 30, index 9, entry 3. Sv39, three levels, which is the same configuration under which objects.rye reads nine object types.
think The first real design finding arrived before any code. A mapping plan needs a place, and regions.rye's Region carries a name and a size and no base. That is correct policy -- two domains may hold the same declaration while the machine puts it in two different places -- and it is a genuine gap for planning. The tempting move was to graft a base onto the declaration. The better move was REDS %122's own lesson: two concerns, two lists. Placement became its own value.
think The second finding came from asking whether greedy is the minimum-page cover or merely a cover. It is the minimum, and structurally rather than empirically: the three page sizes form a divisibility chain, each a whole multiple of the one below by exactly the index width, so declining a larger aligned page that fits can never open a better choice later. It would stop being optimal on a machine offering two sizes neither of which divided the other.
obs The third finding deleted a refusal. The first cut named max_plan_pages at 4096 and added a too_many_pages refusal beside it. Then the arithmetic answered: small pages live only in the fragment before the first megabyte boundary and the fragment after the last, each shorter than one megabyte-page, so at most 511 each; the same argument bounds megabyte-pages by the gigabyte boundaries; gigabyte pages fill the middle and Sv39 addresses 512 of them. The maximum is 2,556, DERIVED rather than chosen -- so the refusal could never fire. An unfireable refusal is worse than an absent one: it reads as a guarded edge while guarding nothing, and no witness can prove it on metal because no input reaches it. The refusal left, the bound became a derivation, and the module refuses four things rather than five. The general rule: when a bound can be derived from the domain, derive it and delete the refusal it would have needed.
obs The sharpest catch of the lap came from the PRINT, not from a witness. The first working cut counted page tables from the placement's extent -- how many aligned spans of each size it crosses -- which sounds sensible and is wrong. A table exists where a page beneath it does. A plan covering a gigabyte, a megabyte-page, and one small page crosses many megabyte spans while holding exactly one small page, so the honest deepest-level count is one. The extent rule said 514. Every assert in the self-test stayed silent, because every one of them was about coverage and refusals and both were correct. What noticed was the table subcommand printing six lines for a human to read, one of them visibly absurd. A module that can print a worked example is a module a reader can catch being wrong, and on this lap the print was the only check that fired. The corrected six-object count is bound by the witness now, so it cannot return quietly.
obs A second self-correction rode along: check_page_bound asserted unreachable on a placement it believed was all-small, and the panic was right -- a 4096-page run one page above a megabyte boundary folds into megabyte-pages almost immediately, so the bound was never approached. My test was wrong, not the code, and the assert said so before any witness ran.
obs The geometry scan found its own gap on first run: one of three page symbols missing. The gigabyte page is declared in the riscv64 MODE header while the megabyte and small pages are declared in the riscv ARCHITECTURE header -- because the gigabyte page is the sole member of the mode tier, which is exactly the width objects.rye already reads as tier_width(.mode) == 1. Two independent readings of the same fact agreeing, and the guard reporting rather than passing.
obs Docs and implementation moved in one commit: objects.rye's reason beside the four owed no longer says nothing yet builds the mapping, since something now plans it exactly. Its assert that the five held are exactly the portable tier is untouched and still holds -- a plan is not a retype.
obs The rung was registered in caravan_suite_witness.rish the same lap it was written, per REDS %81, where nine crypto rungs once landed GREEN and unheard.
obs The ceiling is the honest pressure to name. Carry rose exactly nine -- the byte-identical main this module shares with its neighbors -- leaving five lines of headroom under 87,800. The next module carrying that same main breaches it, which promotes main from the queue's third-largest family to the lift arc's real next crux.
loom witness=caravan_mapping page_sizes=3 levels=3 refusals=4 max_plan_pages_derived=2556 red_paths=3 worked_plan_objects=6
loom scan=caravan_ladder_carry modules=110 carried_lines=87795 ceiling=87800 families=707 delta_lines=9 headroom=5
loom suite=caravan_suite witnesses=107 verdict=GREEN
file caravan/mapping.rye the Sv39 lowering -- a placement to the exact pages and page tables it costs, with the bound derived rather than chosen
file tools/caravan_mapping_witness.rish binds the self-test, the worked plan, and the five numbers read from seL4's header; three RED paths on metal
file tools/fixtures/caravan_mapping_geometry_scan.sh reads five geometry numbers and three page symbols from seL4's own headers and diffs them against what the module prints
file tools/fixtures/caravan_mapping_geometry_control.sh plants a page size moved one bit and proves the module's own asserts refuse it
file caravan/objects.rye the reason beside the four owed now names the plan that exists, docs synced in the same commit
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish registers the new rung, so nothing in the arc goes unheard
file tools/caravan_ladder_carry_witness.rish carry pins moved to the measured truth; ceiling untouched at 87,800 with five lines of headroom
file tools/caravan_ladder_print_witness.rish module count moved 109 to 110; the holding count stays 43, measured rather than assumed
file tools/caravan_ladder_spine_witness.rish module count moved 109 to 110
file active-designing/20260821-222916_the-address-space-debt-and-the-mapping-plan.md the essay -- worth reading with the code deleted
file crux/REMEMBER.md one live-edge row and a fresh Now; the stale Now folded to a pointer at its own log
recommend keep-going main is the crux twice over now -- it leads the ceiling pressure with five lines of headroom left, and it sits third on the carry queue at 64 rungs by 17 lines. Lifting it pays the ladder arc and the ceiling in one move. Beside it, the machine half of the address space stays owed and honestly named: page-table entry bytes, an ASID from seL4_ASIDPoolBits, and the retype itself. The libsel4 generator gate (jinja2, ply) is still Keaton's word and still blocks rungs 3 and 4 of the arc.
